{#
	A list's choice of view (owner, 2026-10-26: "So ADMIN can choose between list view and grid view"): its table or its
	grid of cards, remembered for the reader (Support\ListView). Plain links, so it works without JavaScript; the view shown
	now is the filled button and says so to a screen reader.
	vs: the list's <dataset>_view_switch. With JavaScript the list changes where it is (owner, 2026-10-30: "I don't want
	that. I just want the view of the list of slides to change without a full page reload"): htmx fetches the same address
	and swaps only the list's own area, its toolbar, results and pagination, the element vs_region names (its list's name
	and "-view" unless given), as the list's search does. The choice is remembered by the server as before.
#}
{% set vs_area = '#' ~ (vs_region|default(vs.name ~ '-view')) %}
<div class="cl-view-switch" role="group" aria-label="Show as">
	{{ ui('action.link', {label: 'List', variant: vs.view == 'list' ? 'primary' : 'secondary', size: 'small', href: vs.list_href, get: vs.list_href, target: vs_area, select: vs_area ~ ' > *', id: vs.name ~ '-show-list', icon: 'action-view-list', aria_label: vs.view == 'list' ? 'List, shown now' : 'Show as a list'}) }}
	{{ ui('action.link', {label: 'Grid', variant: vs.view == 'grid' ? 'primary' : 'secondary', size: 'small', href: vs.grid_href, get: vs.grid_href, target: vs_area, select: vs_area ~ ' > *', id: vs.name ~ '-show-grid', icon: 'action-view-grid', aria_label: vs.view == 'grid' ? 'Grid, shown now' : 'Show as a grid of cards'}) }}
</div>
